From: Linux psX contributors
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: add boot-gated bounded SATA diagnostic markers

Observe the Baikal embedded HDD path without changing timeout, reset, IRQ,
PHY or DMA policy. ps4_sata_diag=1 enables timestamped stage observations,
effective DMA masks and mapped SG address ranges. Default is off.

The device filter requires Sony 104d:90de at 0000:00:14.7; per-port markers
use hardware port 0 rather than assuming global ata1 numbering. No disk
payloads, raw IDENTIFY data, model, serial or key material are logged.

Diagnostic delta against the matching 7.2.11 runtime source archive recorded
in BASELINE.json. This patch is deliberately outside all active series.
Compilation and source review do not establish hardware acceptance.

